# Acceptance evidence. Archived by CI as a build artefact, not
# committed: a run directory is a record of one machine at one
# moment, and a repository full of them is a repository nobody can
# tell the current evidence from.
sim/r1/

# Downloaded toolchains, fetched by checksum into the tree so an acceptance
# environment owns its own copy (tools/xls/fetch_xls.sh). Several hundred
# megabytes of somebody else's release; the digest that pins it is in
# tools/xls/config.json, which IS committed.
.xls/
tritonenv/

# Staged for packaging by `make r2-stage-data`; the originals are the
# repository's own spec/, isa/, rtl/, tb/ and tools/asm/.
python/tnca/data/
python/_staged/

# setuptools' build tree. It was committed once, and because build_py only
# recopies a source that is NEWER than its copy, the wheel was then built
# from a months-old snapshot: the shipped transport wrote six mailbox fields
# while the shipped device read eight, and nothing answered. `r2-package`
# deletes it before every build, and r2-package-tests compares the wheel
# against the sources (PKG-06).
build/
